<title>USA: Washington Mutual sees 5 pct accretion.</title>
<headline>Washington Mutual sees 5 pct accretion.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Washington Mutual Savings Bank officials said Thursday the company's proposed merger with Great Western Financial Corp would produce five percent accretion to earnings in 1998.</p>
<p>In a conference call with analysts, the officials also said the deal would produce 11 percent accretion to earnings in 1999.</p>
<p>The two thrifts announced a stock-swap merger pact earlier today.</p>
<p>H.F. Ahmanson and Co has made a hostile bid for Great Western. Ahmanson said today it remained fully committed to its offer.</p>
</text>
